 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Good to hear you. Running specific gear is minimal, a comfortable running shirt and shorts you don't mind getting sweaty in, a good watch, and a light sweater or hoodie for cold post-run chills. For beginner gear, a basic band or dolce is worth the extra price. A basic watch will keep time and track distance, handy for building up and seeing progress. Headlamp is handier than you'd think, and light weight merino running socks are worth it for comfort. Stick to affordable basics, and save up for a half marathon if you stick with long after the New Year's rush has faded.",
